      "post_subject": "model building for holography",
      "content_md": "in my effort to create a truly selfmade hologram , i have be trying to sculpt an extended hand (using sculpey bake clay), its no more than two inches, and no matter what ,it seems to be moving. i even baked it twice ,thinking it was possibly underbaked\n\nthe base comes out bright but the single fingers always move! long settle times, extreme baffeling . im ready to return to plaster sculpting.\n\ni have read here on the forum outhers use it..........",
      "signature": "",
      "attachments": [],
      "quotes": [],
      "is_first_post": true,
      "url": "https://holographyforum.org/forum/viewtopic.php?p=39506#p39506"
    },
